# Always push after changes

After every change to the repository, commit it and push to `origin` (https://github.com/TDKasala/SpazaStock), branch `main`, before ending the turn.

- Run the relevant checks first (`npm run lint`, `npm test`, `npm run build`) and only push when they pass. If they fail, fix the failure or tell the user why nothing was pushed.
- Use a clear commit message that describes what changed.
- Never force-push. If the push is rejected because GitHub has newer commits, `git pull --rebase origin main`, resolve the conflicts, re-run the checks, then push.
- Confirm the push succeeded and tell the user the new commit hash.
- If a turn made no changes, check `git status -sb` and push any unpushed commits.
